#!/usr/bin/python3 -I
"""knk-deploy (Stage B): bounded change operations on the NAS knk-alpha stack for Claude Code on the LAN PC.

Runs as root through sudo, started only by the knk-deploy dispatcher. Every argument is validated here again.
The caller never gets a shell, never chooses a path or a command, and never sees a secret value:
  - code arrives as an upload (stdin) named by its git commit; the PC checks that the commit is on trunk;
  - images are built from NAS-owned build files (/srv/docker/build/<repo>/_files) plus the uploaded source;
  - Compose changes pass a policy check against the running file (no privileges, ports, host paths or secrets
    that weren't there before);
  - config files travel with secret values replaced by <<secret:NAME>> tokens, both ways.
Every change takes a backup first, checks health afterwards and rolls back by itself when health fails.
Database restores stay a manual step (knk-alpha-restore).

Usage (via ssh knk-deploy <command> ...):
  status | compose-get | config-get NAME | logs SERVICE [MINUTES]
  upload api-src|web-src|plugin-jar COMMIT   < file      upload compose|config-NAME SHA256 < file
  deploy-api COMMIT | deploy-web COMMIT | deploy-plugin COMMIT
  compose-apply SHA256 | config-apply NAME SHA256
  snapshot LABEL | restart SERVICE | rollback
"""
